# No JS alert — use modal popups

Do **not** use `window.alert()`, `window.confirm()`, or browser-native dialog boxes for user-facing validation, errors, or notices when a modal can be shown instead.

## Required pattern (POS register / cart)

Use the shared helper in `assets/js/pos_message_modal.js`:

```javascript
window.showPosMessageModal({
  title: 'Customer required',
  message: 'Please select customer first',
  tone: 'warning', // error | warning | info | success
  onClose: function () {
    window.focusPosCustomerSelect && window.focusPosCustomerSelect();
  }
});
```

Load `pos_message_modal.js` before other POS scripts that may call it.

## When alert is allowed

Only when **no DOM / modal is possible**, for example:

- A non-browser runtime (CLI script, pure Node without UI)
- Catastrophic boot failure before any modal markup or helper can load

In that case prefer `console.error` / logging first; use `alert` only as a last resort and note why in a short comment.

## Other UI surfaces

- **POS checkout/cart flows:** modal (`showPosMessageModal`) for blocking validation; toasts optional for non-blocking success/info.
- **Legacy admin pages:** prefer existing app modal/dialog components over `alert` when touching that code.
- **Do not introduce new `alert()` calls** in POS JS (`assets/js/pos*.js`, `views/pos_register/**`).

## Examples

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
alert('Please select customer first');

// ✅ GOOD
showPosMessageModal({
  title: 'Customer required',
  message: 'Please select customer first',
  tone: 'warning',
  onClose: function () { focusPosCustomerSelect(); }
});
```
